    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "A dancer turns $60^\\circ$ nine times, then $40^\\circ$ twelve times, then $90^\\circ$ thirteen times. What angle does he make with his original position? Use modulo arithmetic.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$30^\\circ$",
      "worked": "A full turn is $360^\\circ$, so calculate modulo $360$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}60\\times9+40\\times12+90\\times13&\\equiv180+120+90\\pmod{360}\\\\60\\times9+40\\times12+90\\times13&\\equiv390\\pmod{360}\\\\60\\times9+40\\times12+90\\times13&\\equiv30\\pmod{360}\\end{align*}$$\n\nHe finishes at an angle of $30^\\circ$ to his original position.",
